.TH LEER 8 "2026-08-25" "leer 0.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
leer \- user configuration snapshot & selective restore tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B leer
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B leer
creates versioned, hardlink-deduplicated snapshots of user configuration
(\fI~/.config\fR including per-app directories, \fI~/.themes\fR,
\fI~/.icons\fR, \fI~/.fonts\fR, and top-level dotfiles), plus \fI/etc\fR and
package/service manifests. Restores are selective: pick exactly which files
or application directories to roll back via a GUI checklist (zenity) or a
numbered terminal menu.
.PP
leer is fully manual \(en it never runs automatically, never touches pacman
transactions, and never registers bootloader entries.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B snap "\fR[\fI\--tag MSG\fR]\fP" "\fR[\fI\--quiet\fR]\fP"
Create a snapshot. Requires root.
.TP
.B list
List all snapshots with date, tag and size.
.TP
.B diff "\fIid1\fR" "\fR[\fBid2|live\fR]\fP"
Compare two snapshots, or a snapshot against the live system.
.TP
.B restore "\fIid\fR" "\fR[\fI\--pick\fR]\fP" "\fR[\fI\--yes\fR]\fP"
Restore a snapshot. With \fI\--pick\fR an interactive chooser lists every
captured item (per-app directories under .config, individual dotfiles,
theme dirs, /etc as one unit). Items differing from the live system are
pre-checked with change counts; untick anything you want left alone.
Without a display (TTY/SSH recovery) the same list appears as a numbered
menu. A dry-run plan is shown before anything is written. Deletions are
scoped to selected paths only \(em caches, histories and unrelated files
are never touched. Requires root.
.TP
.B drop "\fIid\fR" "\fR[\fI\--yes\fR]\fP"
Delete one specific snapshot permanently (refuses the last remaining one).
.TP
.B prune "\fR[\fIkeep-n\fR]\fP"
Delete oldest snapshots beyond \fIkeep-n\fR.
.TP
.B schedule "RstatusP | set IpresetR | set R\-\-atI exprR | off"
Manage automatic snapshots via a systemd timer. Presets: hourly, daily,
weekly, monthly, yearly; I\-\-atR accepts any systemd OnCalendar
expression. Scheduled runs are tagged BautoR and obey retention.
Requires root to change.
.TP
.B gui
Graphical hub (zenity): create snapshot, restore (snapshot dropdown plus
the interactive file chooser), edit the schedule, drop/prune snapshots,
run doctor. Root actions elevate via pkexec.
.TP
.B doctor
Verify dependencies, storage, configuration and schedule state.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/leer.conf
Retention, storage location, home paths, theme-dir toggle, exclude patterns.
.TP
.I /var/lib/leer/snapshots/<id>/
MANIFEST, home/, etc/, meta/ (package lists, enabled services).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, non-zero on error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rsync (1),
.BR zenity (1)
